# ACADEMIC SYSTEM PRIORITY

This application manages:
- student progress
- grades
- scores
- educational analytics
- evaluations

These systems are HIGH PRIORITY and HIGH SENSITIVITY.

# IMPORTANT

Never modify grading logic irresponsibly.

Never break:
- score calculations
- averages
- student history
- progression tracking
- achievement systems
- report generation

# STUDENT DATA

Student-related data must be:
- accurate
- protected
- consistent
- traceable

# GRADE SYSTEMS

All grading systems should:
- be deterministic
- avoid random inconsistencies
- preserve history
- support auditability

# EDUCATIONAL ANALYTICS

Prefer systems that:
- track improvement
- monitor progression
- identify learning patterns
- encourage motivation

# UX FOR STUDENTS

Academic systems should feel:
- motivating
- rewarding
- understandable
- encouraging

Avoid:
- harsh punishment systems
- negative emotional feedback
- demotivating language

# TEACHER/ADMIN PANELS

Admin interfaces should prioritize:
- clarity
- efficiency
- organization
- fast access to information
- visual summaries

# DATA VISUALIZATION

Prefer:
- charts
- progress bars
- visual analytics
- performance summaries
- achievement indicators

# SAFETY

Never:
- delete student progress
- overwrite grades
- reset progress systems

without explicit approval.

# ARCHITECTURE

Academic logic should remain:
- modular
- testable
- isolated
- scalable